<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      The per-strategy field block the EOD downtrend detector stamps on every
      trade_config it generates.

      What this replaces
      ==================
      EodDowntrendDetectionService.strategyDefaults(int) was a hardcoded switch:

          case 1: return new StrategyDefaults("SELL", 1, 200, 1, 1);
          default: return null;

      Two problems with that. First, transaction_type / max_loss / no_of_trades /
      no_of_parrellel_trades decide when a trade enters and how many fire, so per
      CLAUDE.md #9 they are trading behaviour and must come from config, not from a
      service constant. Second - and this is what actually blocked the feature -
      the `default: return null` branch made processRule skip the rule outright, so
      tagging a rule with any strategy other than 1 silently generated nothing.

      Adding a strategy to the auto-config pipeline is now an INSERT here, not a
      redeploy.

      auto_config_enabled
      ===================
      Lets a strategy be parked without deleting its block. A rule tagged with a
      disabled strategy is skipped with a warning that names it - never silently.

      Seeded with strategy 1 only
      ===========================
      The values below are lifted verbatim from the switch being deleted, so
      behaviour on an existing database is unchanged. Strategy 2 deliberately gets
      NO row: its max_loss / no_of_trades / no_of_parrellel_trades are trading
      decisions nobody has made yet, and CLAUDE.md #9 forbids guessing a default
      for them. Until someone inserts that row the detector logs

          rule id=N - strategy 2 has no strategy_defaults row, skipping

      which is the correct loud failure. Adding it is one INSERT:

          INSERT INTO strategy_defaults
            (strategy_id, transaction_type, lot_quantity, max_loss,
             no_of_trades, no_of_parallel_trades, auto_config_enabled)
          VALUES (2, 'SELL', 1, <max_loss>, <trades>, <parallel>, TRUE);
    -->
    <changeSet id="033_create_strategy_defaults" author="moneymaker">
        <createTable tableName="strategy_defaults">
            <column name="strategy_id" type="INT">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="transaction_type" type="VARCHAR(8)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- Last-resort fallback only. The generated config takes its quantity
                 from instrument.lot_qty when that is set, because NFO accepts whole
                 lots and the contract is what defines one. -->
            <column name="lot_quantity" type="INT">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="max_loss" type="DECIMAL(12,4)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="no_of_trades" type="INT">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="no_of_parallel_trades" type="INT">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="auto_config_enabled" type="BOOLEAN" defaultValueBoolean="true">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="033_seed_strategy_defaults_strategy1" author="moneymaker">
        <insert tableName="strategy_defaults">
            <column name="strategy_id" valueNumeric="1"/>
            <column name="transaction_type" value="SELL"/>
            <column name="lot_quantity" valueNumeric="1"/>
            <column name="max_loss" valueNumeric="200"/>
            <column name="no_of_trades" valueNumeric="1"/>
            <column name="no_of_parallel_trades" valueNumeric="1"/>
            <column name="auto_config_enabled" valueBoolean="true"/>
        </insert>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
